my Top 5 moments and then I'll  do my review.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.800
So everybody grab a spoon and get some
others pudding! Number 5

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.460
Michonne eulogizes Hershel. In my
mind she just went back to the prison to

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.890
see what had happened since that
midseason finale

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:46.010
and happened upon Hershel. She wasn't
ONLY looking for him.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:48.980
In a way though she did give him the
final peace that he deserved. who was

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:51.149
really touching given what The Governor
did.

00:00:51.149 --> 00:00:54.440
Speaking of which, we actually finally saw
that gunshot wound.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.850
Greg Nicotero actually ended up bringing
that Animatronic Hershel head to

00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:58.690
Talking Dead.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:01.859
Remember that time on Talking Dead when
Chris Hardwick tried to feed pudding to

00:01:01.859 --> 00:01:03.109
that dead Hershel head?

00:01:03.109 --> 00:01:06.869
SO WRONG. Number 4 - Carl almost has to
kill Rick.

00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:10.409
Next to Carl getting buried beneath a
pile walkers this was one of the most

00:01:10.409 --> 00:01:12.250
intense moments in the episode.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:15.560
Which is why I chose it over to the
other close calls that Carl had.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:18.340
Watching Carl just break at the thought of having to kill his dad

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.340
was so horrifying. Rick had actually been
making those Weezy Walker sounds the

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:23.320
entire episode.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:26.729
He was so beat up he looked and moved
like a walker too.

00:01:26.729 --> 00:01:30.100
This fake out moment was just the
payoff to that. I kept thinking there were

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:33.299
walkers just around the corner where
ever they went. But it was always just

00:01:33.299 --> 00:01:37.380
Rick making those sounds. Number 3 -
Michonne's flashback dream sequence.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:40.810
This was the most beautifully shot scene
in the episode. Michonne had really

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:42.950
reverted her season 3 personality.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:46.390
You know the coping mechanism of just
shutting everything down and taking pets.

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:49.470
The dream sequence was just her way of
processing what had happened.

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:52.149
And I don't know what would have
happened had she not known about Carl

00:01:52.149 --> 00:01:53.280
and Rick's footprints.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:56.320
If you can catch the reference, those
two water pets that Michonne had at the

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:59.149
beginning of the episode were just
visual metaphors for Mike and Terry.

00:01:59.149 --> 00:02:03.610
You know the men she lost. Number 2 - Carl
finally has it out with a comatose Rick.

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:07.450
I think having Rick passed out the whole
time sped Carl up to that breaking point

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:08.550
where he could just verbalize

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:12.330
all the things he was angry about. Yes, he
did say some very awful things.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:15.599
But he wasn't actually mad at Rick. At
least not in the way he made it sound.

00:02:15.599 --> 00:02:18.660
He's just expressing all the rage and
frustration that's built up over the

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:19.760
past 3 seasons.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:22.670
All the friends and family they lost, you
know their entire way of life being

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:23.540
destroyed.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:26.580
This has really been my favorite scene
with the two of them together. They've had a

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:29.520
couple moments together this season, but
none that were this intense.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:33.730
Just let it out Carl, just let it out.
It's okay to cry. And my Number 1 moment -

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:35.459
Carl gets his victory pudding!

00:02:35.459 --> 00:02:38.519
This was Carl's big moment of triumph,
you know, a big reaffirmation.

00:02:38.519 --> 00:02:42.120
He said "I Win" twice during the episode
and this was the second time.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:45.890
Everyone had lost so much that the chalk
on the door and that pudding on the roof

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:49.239
was just a way for him to take
something back, to get at least one big

00:02:49.239 --> 00:02:49.800
win.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:53.830
I mean seriously, Michonne had this
amazing trip, you know, back to reality.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:57.120
But his was really Carl's episode. What is
his future though?

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:00.590
Is he going to end up turning into
someone like Michonne? She did just knock

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:02.110
on the door at the end of the episode

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:05.180
and Rick said, you know, "It's for you". So
clearly he's going to be spending a lot

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:06.280
of time with her.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:09.030
It was such an amazing episode though,
let me know what your

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:09.519
favorite moment was!

00:03:09.519 --> 00:03:12.670
As a midseason premiere I have to give
this a solid "A".

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:16.180
You know, largely due to Chandler Riggs
being so awesome in it. And the deep dive

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.569
into Michonne, which we haven't gotten
in a long time.

00:03:18.569 --> 00:03:22.709
The story was a direct adaptation of
issues 49 and 50 the comic book too.

00:03:22.709 --> 00:03:25.849
The stories are always informed by the comic, but this was actually a literal

00:03:25.849 --> 00:03:27.069
beat for beat adaptation.

00:03:27.069 --> 00:03:30.730
Hershel's funeral was a great payoff for
the fandom. I had so many questions on my

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:32.060
Walking Dead videos since

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:35.349
episode 8, about how Herschel would
totally be a walker. It's a sentence

00:03:35.349 --> 00:03:38.670
that's worse than death, so it was really
nice to see him laid to rest.

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:42.260
Speaking of which, it was really nice to
finally get an answer on The Governor.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:45.360
A lot of people bet me that he would
totally show up as a walker, but when we

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:46.739
saw the gunshot wound in his head,

00:03:46.739 --> 00:03:50.090
we totally got our answer. I was a little
disappointed that we did not get to see

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:50.849
baby Judith.

00:03:50.849 --> 00:03:54.129
Robert Kirkman actually said we would
get a definitive answer about her

00:03:54.129 --> 00:03:54.700
very soon.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:58.290
Nicotero actually did imply that we
would see The Governor again before the

00:03:58.290 --> 00:03:59.129
season finale.

00:03:59.129 --> 00:04:02.250
But obviously knowing what we know now,
he'll probably just be a hallucination.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:05.510
I can't say enough about the stylistic
choices in the episode though, when

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:06.900
Michonne was mowing down her

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:10.299
heard of Walker's, the camera panned out,
you know, to reveal this neat

00:04:10.299 --> 00:04:11.060
little circle

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:14.209
It looked just like the dead Night's
Watchmen circle that the White Walkers

00:04:14.209 --> 00:04:17.299
left for Jon Snow during Season 3 of Game
of Thrones.

00:04:17.299 --> 00:04:20.729
Great story, great style. It's really
gonna be hard to top this next week.

00:04:20.729 --> 00:04:23.199
the good news is that we will pick up
with the group we didn't see in this

00:04:23.199 --> 00:04:26.160
episode so I'm crossing my fingers we
will see baby Judith.

